  "context_pill": "Basic Concepts, Tax Rates and Exempt Income",
  "example_summary": "Comparing tax liability under partial integration scheme for Mr. X at age 40 versus age 75 under the old tax regime.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Summary Matrix: Partial Integration Scheme\n\n| Provision / Section | Statutory Condition / Limit | Tax Treatment / Legal Consequence |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Section 10(1)** | Agricultural income as defined u/s 2(1A) | 100% Exempt from Income Tax |\n| **Net Agri Income Computation** | Gross Agricultural Receipts *less* Revenue Expenditure | Expenses incurred exclusively for agri income are deductible |\n| **Partial Integration Condition 1** | Net Agricultural Income exceeds **₹ 5,000 p.a.** | Mandatory trigger for partial integration |\n| **Partial Integration Condition 2** | Non-Agricultural Income exceeds **Basic Exemption Limit** | Mandatory trigger for partial integration |\n| **Basic Exemption Limit (Age < 60)** | Resident Individual aged below 60 years | **₹ 2,50,000** |\n| **Basic Exemption Limit (Age 60 to <80)** | Resident Senior Citizen | **₹ 3,00,000** |\n\n\n### Step-by-Step Partial Integration Computation Framework\n\n* **Step 1:** Calculate Income Tax on (**Total Non-Agricultural Income + Net Agricultural Income**) at standard slab rates.\n* **Step 2:** Calculate Income Tax on (**Basic Exemption Limit + Net Agricultural Income**) at standard slab rates.\n* **Step 3:** Subtract tax computed in **Step 2** from tax computed in **Step 1** ($Tax_{Step 1} - Tax_{Step 2}$).\n* **Step 4 & 5:** Add **Health and Education Cess @ 4%** on the resulting net tax payable to arrive at final tax liability.\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Regime Applicability:** Partial integration applies when an Assessee opts out of the default tax regime u/s 115BAC and is assessed under the optional/old tax regime provisions.",
